---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer — SeedMask"
  description="Trademark notices and product disclaimers for SeedMask hardware, firmware, and Coordinator."
>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero-learn">
    <div class="container learn-article-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p>Trademarks, product status, and the limits of what SeedMask claims.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container prose learn-prose">
      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Ledger, OneKey, Google, Facebook, and other marks are trademarks of their owners. Used only to identify
        devices or websites. SeedMask is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bitcoin, Kaspa, Apple, Google, Android, iOS, and any other third-party names or logos that appear in SeedMask
        software or on this website are likewise the property of their respective owners and are used only for
        identification. Nothing on this site or in the product constitutes a partnership, sponsorship, certification,
        or endorsement by those owners.
      </p>

      <h2>Product status</h2>
      <p>
        SeedMask hardware, firmware, and the SeedMask Coordinator are early-stage products. Features described on this
        website may be incomplete, change without notice, or ship later than indicated. “Coming soon” means the item is
        not generally available yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        SeedMask Coordinator and related software have <strong>not completed a third-party security audit</strong> and
        may contain bugs, errors, omissions, or incomplete behavior. Do not treat them as production-ready custody
        software until independent review and product maturity catch up.
      </p>

      <h2>No custody guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        Self-custody means <strong>you</strong> are responsible for your seeds, passphrases, PINs, backup codes,
        passwords, devices, and recovery practices. SeedMask provides tools; it does not custody your assets, reverse
        transactions, or recover funds lost because of forgotten secrets, lost backups, malware on your everyday
        computers, physical theft, social engineering, or user error.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always confirm amounts and destinations on the SeedMask device screen before approving. Fast networks and
        polished interfaces do not change that rule.
      </p>

      <h2>No investment or legal advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this website or in SeedMask software is investment, tax, accounting, or legal advice. Cryptocurrency
        involves risk of total loss. Educate yourself and, where appropriate, consult qualified professionals.
      </p>

      <h2>Software and documentation</h2>
      <p>
        Firmware, Coordinator builds, documentation, and tutorials are provided <strong>as is</strong>, without
        warranties of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement, to
        the fullest extent permitted by law. SeedMask is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
        punitive damages, or for loss of cryptoassets, data, profits, or business, arising from use of the products or
        this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prefer test amounts and known-good networks while you learn the workflow. Verify release hashes and sources
        whenever you install software that participates in your custody path.
      </p>

      <h2>Open source</h2>
      <p>
        Where SeedMask publishes source code, transparency enables review — it does not by itself guarantee safety,
        correctness, or freedom from vulnerabilities. Always verify what you run.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top: 36px">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/about">← About</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
